<BaseLayout title="About | Kiden Scruton" description="Kiden Scruton: an aerospace engineering background with experience in hardware development, testing, fabrication, and team leadership.">
 <div class="about-page">
 <header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">About me</p><h1>I like making ideas work in the real world.</h1><p class="intro">My background is in aerospace engineering at the University of Hartford. My strongest interest is hardware: mechanical design, electronics, and the process of building and testing physical prototypes.</p></header>
 <div class="about-intro"><article class="prose"><h2>The hardware is what draws me in.</h2><p>The Brennan-inspired monorail is one of the projects I care most about. Bringing together flywheels, motors, mounts, sensing, and control made it an especially demanding build.</p><p>That is the kind of work I want this portfolio to show: making physical parts fit and behave together, then finding out where the model and the hardware disagree. Code and simulation are part of that process.</p><p>The monorail did not reach reliable stabilization. It still represents a substantial part of my work, from mechanical design and parts selection to wiring and Arduino control.</p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/brennan-gyro-monorail/">Explore the monorail build →</a></article><aside class="about-focus"><p class="eyebrow">What I want to work on</p><h2>Mechanisms and working prototypes.</h2><p>I’m interested in work that puts mechanical design, electronics, fabrication, and testing in the same process, with aerospace as an important part of my background.</p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">See the hardware projects →</a></aside></div>
 <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="experience-title"><div class="section-top"><div><p class="eyebrow">Experience in practice</p><h2 id="experience-title">Across the lab and the workbench.</h2></div></div><div class="about-experience">{experience.map(item=><article><p class="eyebrow">{item.url ? <a href={item.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{item.company} ↗</a> : item.company}</p><h3>{item.role}</h3><p>{item.description}</p><p>{experienceDetails[item.company as keyof typeof experienceDetails]}</p></article>)}</div></section>
 <section class="about-intro section-block leadership-stories" aria-labelledby="leadership-title"><article class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Working with people</p><h2 id="leadership-title">Taking responsibility beyond my own part.</h2><div class="leadership-story"><h3>From RockOn! to RockSat-C</h3><p>The Connecticut Space Grant Consortium helped make two Wallops Flight Facility experiences possible for me: RockOn! first, then RockSat-C. After proving myself alongside Nick Krupa in RockOn!, I went on to co-lead the University of Hartford's first participation in RockSat-C. I helped coordinate technical work, timelines, procurement, and budgets alongside payload development. The 2025 mission completed launch, recovery, and data collection, and I was part of the launch team.</p></div><div class="leadership-story"><h3>Building a chapter from the ground up</h3><p>As founding president, I built the University of Hartford Kappa Sigma organization from nothing alongside two of my best friends. We developed recruitment and organizational processes, led events, and supported philanthropy. Earning our charter in January 2026 cemented the chapter’s status and made that shared effort a lasting part of the university. More than 40 members of our chapter have now graduated from the University of Hartford.</p><a class="text-link instagram-link" href="https://www.instagram.com/uhartkapsig/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chapter Instagram · @uhartkapsig ↗</a></div><div class="leadership-story"><h3>A family business, built together</h3><p>Before university, my family and I built Scruton Brother’s Ice Cream from the ground up in Southern Pines, North Carolina. The restaurant operated for three years before closing in 2023. My brother and I ran daily operations. My own food allergies helped shape our dairy-free and gluten-free options; hands-on refrigeration troubleshooting and supply logistics taught me how to keep a business running.</p><a class="text-link instagram-link" href="https://www.instagram.com/scrutonbrothersicecream/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Family business Instagram · @scrutonbrothersicecream ↗</a></div></article><aside class="about-focus"><p class="eyebrow">Away from the desk</p><h2>Still making things.</h2><p>I enjoy model rocketry and airplane building, DIY electronics, custom computers, welding, and automotive maintenance. Outside the workshop, my interests include hiking, off-roading, and golf.</p><div class="sidebar-chapter"><h3>Kappa Sigma · Phi Kappa</h3><div class="family-gallery chapter-gallery"><figure><a href="/assets/chapter-founders.jpg" data-lightbox data-caption="Ryan, Aidan, and me with our chapter charter."><img src="/assets/chapter-founders.jpg" alt="The three chapter founders in suits holding the framed Kappa Sigma charter." width="1170" height="877" loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption>Ryan, Aidan, and me with our charter.</figcaption></figure><figure><a href="/assets/chapter-charter-event.jpg" data-lightbox data-caption="Phi Kappa brothers celebrating the chapter’s charter at the University of Hartford."><img src="/assets/chapter-charter-event.jpg" alt="Phi Kappa brothers gathered with their charter at the University of Hartford chapter event." width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption>Celebrating our chapter’s charter.</figcaption></figure></div></div><div class="sidebar-family"><h3>Scruton Brother’s Ice Cream</h3><div class="family-gallery"><figure><a href="/assets/scruton-family.jpg" data-lightbox data-caption="Our family at Scruton Brother’s Ice Cream."><img src="/assets/scruton-family.jpg" alt="The Scruton family together inside their ice cream restaurant." loading="lazy" width="640" height="640" /></a><figcaption>A business we built as a family.</figcaption></figure><figure><a href="/assets/scruton-storefront.jpg" data-lightbox data-caption="The Scruton Brother’s Ice Cream storefront in Southern Pines, North Carolina."><img src="/assets/scruton-storefront.jpg" alt="Blue Scruton Brother’s Ice Cream storefront with the restaurant sign above the entrance." loading="lazy" width="640" height="480" /></a><figcaption>Our storefront in Southern Pines, NC.</figcaption></figure></div></div></aside></section>
